🧬 Reference-Based Genome Assembly Pipeline (Rice)
📦 With Installation + Commands + Purpose
🔰 Step 0: Install Required Tools

Command:

sudo apt update

# Core tools
sudo apt install -y bwa samtools bcftools bedtools seqtk emboss

# Read simulator
sudo apt install -y art-nextgen-simulation-tools

# Compression tools
sudo apt install -y tabix

# BLAST
sudo apt install -y ncbi-blast+

Purpose:
Install all software required for genome assembly, SNP detection, and annotation.

🔰 Step 1: Create Working Directory

Command:

mkdir Genome_Assembly
cd Genome_Assembly

Purpose:
Organize all files in one place.

🌾 Step 2: Download Reference Genome

Command:

wget https://ftp.ensemblgenomes.ebi.ac.uk/pub/plants/release-56/fasta/oryza_sativa/dna/Oryza_sativa.IRGSP-1.0.dna.toplevel.fa.gz
gunzip *.gz
mv Oryza_sativa.IRGSP-1.0.dna.toplevel.fa rice.fa

Purpose:
Provides base genome for alignment.

🧬 Step 3: Download Annotation File

Command:

wget https://ftp.ensemblgenomes.ebi.ac.uk/pub/plants/release-56/gff3/oryza_sativa/Oryza_sativa.IRGSP-1.0.56.gff3.gz
gunzip *.gz
mv Oryza_sativa.IRGSP-1.0.56.gff3 rice.gff3

Purpose:
Used to extract genes later.

🧪 Step 4: Generate Mutated Genome (SNP Simulation)

Command:

seqtk mutfa -r 0.001 rice.fa > rice_mut.fa

Purpose:
Introduce SNPs artificially.

🔬 Step 5: Simulate Sequencing Reads

Command:

art_illumina -ss HS25 -i rice.fa -p -l 150 -f 5 -o ref
art_illumina -ss HS25 -i rice_mut.fa -p -l 150 -f 5 -o mut

Purpose:
Generate paired-end reads like real sequencing.

⚙️ Step 6: Index Reference Genome

Command:

bwa index rice.fa

Purpose:
Prepare genome for fast mapping.

🔗 Step 7: Align Reads to Reference

Command:

bwa mem -t 4 rice.fa mut1.fq.gz mut2.fq.gz > rice_mut.sam

Purpose:
Map reads to reference genome.

📦 Step 8: Convert SAM to BAM and Sort

Command:

samtools view -Sb rice_mut.sam | samtools sort -o rice_mut.bam

Purpose:
Compress and organize alignment.

📌 Step 9: Index BAM File

Command:

samtools index rice_mut.bam

Purpose:
Enable fast access and visualization.

🧬 Step 10: Variant Calling (SNP Detection)

Command:

bcftools mpileup -f rice.fa rice_mut.bam | bcftools call -mv -Ov -o variants.vcf

Purpose:
Detect SNPs and small variants.

🧾 Step 11: Compress and Index VCF

Command:

bgzip variants.vcf
tabix -p vcf variants.vcf.gz

Purpose:
Prepare VCF for efficient processing.

🧬 Step 12: Generate Consensus Genome

Command:

cat rice.fa | bcftools consensus variants.vcf.gz > assembled_genome.fa

Purpose:
Create final genome sequence.

🧬 Step 13: Extract Gene Sequences

Command:

bedtools getfasta -fi assembled_genome.fa -bed rice.gff3 -fo genes.fa

Purpose:
Extract genes from genome.

🔄 Step 14: Translate to Protein

Command:

transeq genes.fa proteins.fa

Purpose:
Convert DNA → protein sequences.

🔍 Step 15: Download Protein Database

Command:

wget https://ftp.uniprot.org/pub/databases/uniprot/current_release/knowledgebase/complete/uniprot_sprot.fasta.gz
gunzip uniprot_sprot.fasta.gz

Purpose:
Provides reference proteins for annotation.

🔍 Step 16: Functional Annotation (BLAST)

Command:

makeblastdb -in uniprot_sprot.fasta -dbtype prot
blastp -query proteins.fa -db uniprot_sprot.fasta -out results.txt -outfmt 6 -evalue 1e-5 -num_threads 4

Purpose:
Identify protein function.

🖥️ Step 17: Visualization (IGV)

Command (conceptual):

Load rice.fa, rice_mut.bam, variants.vcf.gz in IGV

Purpose:
Validate SNPs visually.

🎯 FINAL OUTPUT FILES
File	Description
rice_mut.bam	Alignment
variants.vcf.gz	SNPs
assembled_genome.fa	Final genome
genes.fa	Gene sequences
proteins.fa	Proteins
results.txt	Annotation
🧠 FINAL CONCEPT

👉 Reference Genome + Reads → Alignment → SNP Detection → Genome Reconstruction → Annotation
